Description: Write and Tables on scaled screens
 Follows wildos-ui-polish. The ribbon, the style cards, the sheet tabs and
 the formula bar drew their sizes in device pixels, so on a scaled screen
 (a 4K laptop at 250 %) the text grew while File, the tab row, the search
 field and the cards stayed small and the font name box showed one letter.
 Their sizes are now the boards' pixels times the screen's scale.
 Margins and box spacing from a .ui, and the width a .ui gives a toolbox
 item, are scaled the same way, as GTK scales its own; at 100 % nothing
 changes.
 From 150 % the sidebar's strip is at least 40 px scaled, since it was
 measured before its icons arrived at the scaled size and cut them in
 half, and a narrower width saved earlier is widened to it.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed
